TITLE:: SDGInsert
summary:: an insert effect on one orbit of a SuperDirtGUI: an eq, a compressor, an insight or a VST plugin, before the orbit's fader
categories:: Libraries>SuperDirtGUI
related:: Classes/SuperDirtGUI, Classes/SDGWindow, Classes/GlobalDirtEffect, Classes/DirtOrbit

DESCRIPTION::
What a channel of a desk calls an insert: an effect in the orbit's own chain,
before its fader, in an order you choose, as many as you like. Four kinds,
each the work of another extension, looked up by name and offered only when it
is installed:

table::
## strong::kind:: || strong::extension:: || strong::what it does on the orbit::
## code::\eq:: || ParaEQ || five bands and two cuts, through code::ParaEQ.ar::
## code::\compressor:: || Compressor || downward or upward compression, through code::Compressor.ar::
## code::\insight:: || Insight || nothing: it copies the orbit's signal, at that point, to a bus an Insight reads
## code::\vst:: || VSTPlugin || whatever the VST plugin does, with its own editor
::

They are made, moved and taken out by the link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI::, which
keeps them per orbit; an insert itself is what you open, bypass and set.

code::
i = ~sdg.addInsert(0, \eq);           // orbit 0, after its other inserts
i.gui;                                // the eq's own window
i.unit.preset = \warm;                // the ParaEQ itself
i.enabled = false;                    // bypassed
c = ~sdg.addInsert(0, \compressor, 0);   // in front of the eq
~sdg.moveInsert(c, 1);                // behind it again
~sdg.insertsOf(0);                    // -> [ SDGInsert(eq, orbit 0, bypassed), SDGInsert(compressor, ...) ]
~sdg.removeInsert(i);
::

An insert can also sit on a track, before or after a global effect:
link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-addTrackInsert:: and link::Classes/SDGTrack::.

In the window: + insert on a strip, or add on the effects tab, then a click on
an insert for its window and a right click to bypass, move or remove it.

subsection:: VST plugins

A code::\vst:: insert hosts one VST2 or VST3 effect through the VSTPlugin
extension. Its plugin is named when it is made - a name VSTPlugin's search found
(link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-vstPlugins::) or a file path - and a click on it in
the window shows the plugin's own editor, or VSTPlugin's generic one for a
plugin without.

code::
v = ~sdg.addInsert(0, \vst, plugin: "ValhallaSupermassive");
v.gui;                                // the plugin's editor
v.genericGui;                         // its parameters as sliders
v.controller.set(0, 0.5);             // its VSTPluginController
::

It is the one insert that is not one of SuperDirt's effects. A plugin lives in
the synth that hosts it, and SuperDirt replaces an orbit's effect synths every
time it rebuilds the orbit - which would close the plugin and lose what was set
in it. So a VST insert is a synth of its own, which SuperDirtGUI walks back into
its place after every rebuild it makes or sees (link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-orderInserts::):
the plugin is never closed by a reload, by the window opening, by a change of
output bus. It never sleeps either - a plugin may make sound out of silence,
and nothing would wake it - so it costs what the plugin costs for as long as it
is in.

Only a cmd-period frees it. The insert is then made again and the plugin
reopened with the state it last read back, which it does by itself a moment
after anything is changed in the plugin's editor, and when asked
(link::#-rememberState::). Bypassed, it uses VSTPlugin's soft bypass: a
crossfade, with a reverb's tail left to fade.

subsection:: Where it sits, and why it stays there

Every insert but a VST one is a link::Classes/GlobalDirtEffect:: of SuperDirt's own kind,
put into the orbit's code::globalEffects:: after SuperDirt's delay, reverb and
leslie and before the add-on's fader - pre-fader, as on a desk, so the meters
and the fader come after it. SuperDirt therefore keeps it in its place through
every rebuild of the orbit: a reload, the window opening, a change of output
bus, cmd-period.

Its synth hears the orbit's two busses as one. Dry and effect are summed - the
sum SuperDirt's monitor makes anyway - processed, and written to the dry bus,
the effect bus cleared. Taking an insert out crossfades the two busses back to
what they were. Like SuperDirt's own effects it sleeps after four seconds of
silence and every event wakes it.

subsection:: Driven by its own extension

The DSP is the extension's pseudo-UGen and the object that drives it is the
extension's own object, in driver mode, aimed at the insert - so the window,
the presets, the clipboard and the meters are theirs, unchanged. What the
object sends lands in the effect's state as well as on its synth, so a synth
SuperDirt starts again begins with the settings the last one had; an eq set
before a reload is the same eq after it.

A compressor's external sidechain is wired by the insert: choose a bus in the
compressor's window and the insert's synth reads it. The eq's spectrum is read
on the orbit's dry bus at the tail of SuperDirt's group: the orbit after all
its inserts and its fader.

An insight insert only reads. Its Insight is named code::orbit<n>_insight<m>::
and its window shows the orbit at the insert's place in the chain. There is
nothing to bypass.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: kindNames
code::[\eq, \compressor, \insight, \vst]::, then the installed link::Classes/FxParamUnit::
subclasses, then the reverbs, in the order a menu lists them.

METHOD:: fxKindNames
The kinds that are link::Classes/FxParamUnit:: subclasses but not reverbs (Growl, Tunnel
and the rest), the window's strong::fx:: submenu.

METHOD:: reverbKindNames
The reverb kinds (Hall, Plate, Coil, Shimmer of sc-reverbs, told apart by their display,
ReverbView), the window's strong::reverb:: submenu.

METHOD:: kinds
The kinds, as an IdentityDictionary from kind to an Event with code::label::,
code::className:: and code::controlName::.

METHOD:: kindLabel
What a strip writes on a kind's button: code::"EQ"::, code::"Comp"::,
code::"Insight"::, code::"VST":: - a VST insert shows its plugin's name instead.
ARGUMENT:: kind
a Symbol.

METHOD:: available
Whether the extension a kind needs is installed.
ARGUMENT:: kind
a Symbol.

METHOD:: availableKinds
The kinds whose extension is installed.

METHOD:: effectName
The name of a kind's GlobalDirtEffect, code::sdgins_<kind>::; its SynthDef
adds the channel count.
ARGUMENT:: kind
a Symbol.

METHOD:: isInsertName
Whether a global effect's name is an insert's.
ARGUMENT:: name
a Symbol or String.

METHOD:: makeDef
The insert's SynthDef for a channel count, or nil when the kind's extension is
not installed. link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-addInsert:: adds it the first time
it is needed.
ARGUMENT:: kind
a Symbol.
ARGUMENT:: numChannels
SuperDirt's channel count.

METHOD:: new
Made by link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-addInsert::, which also puts it into the
orbit; making one by hand puts it nowhere.
ARGUMENT:: sdg
the link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI::.
ARGUMENT:: orbitIndex
the orbit, 0 for the first.
ARGUMENT:: kind
a Symbol, see link::#*kindNames::.
ARGUMENT:: label
what its window calls it.
ARGUMENT:: plugin
a VST insert's plugin: a name VSTPlugin's search found, or a file path.


INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: gui
Open its window: the eq's, the compressor's or the insight's.

METHOD:: enabled
Whether it is in. A bypassed eq or compressor crossfades to the signal it was
given; an insight is always in. Setting it is the same as the switch in the
effect's own window.

METHOD:: canBypass
False for an insight, which only reads.

METHOD:: isVST
Whether it hosts a VST plugin.

METHOD:: node
Its node on the server: the effect's synth, or a VST insert's own.

METHOD:: unit
The link::Classes/ParaEQ:: or Compressor that drives it, or nil for an insight.

METHOD:: insight
The Insight that reads it, or nil.

METHOD:: tapBus
The bus an insight insert copies the orbit to, or nil.

METHOD:: plugin
A VST insert's plugin, as it was named.

METHOD:: controller
A VST insert's VSTPluginController, or nil until the synth is up.

METHOD:: synth
A VST insert's synth.

METHOD:: genericGui
A VST insert's parameters as sliders: VSTPlugin's generic window.

METHOD:: rememberState
Read a VST plugin's state back now and keep it, to reopen the plugin with after
a cmd-period. It happens on its own a second and a half after the last change in
the plugin's editor.
ARGUMENT:: action
called with the data, an Int8Array, or nil when there was nothing to read.

METHOD:: stateData
What link::#-rememberState:: read last.

METHOD:: fx
Its link::Classes/GlobalDirtEffect::.

METHOD:: kind
METHOD:: orbitIndex
METHOD:: orbit
METHOD:: label
METHOD:: shortLabel
METHOD:: number
What it is and where: the kind, the orbit's index and link::Classes/DirtOrbit::,
its window's name, its button's text, and a number counting every insert made.

METHOD:: sdg
METHOD:: server
METHOD:: numChannels
The loader, its server and its channel count.

METHOD:: free
Free its object, window, insight and bus. link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-removeInsert::
calls this after taking the effect out of the orbit; call that instead.


EXAMPLES::

code::
// after ~dirt.start and ~sdg = SuperDirtGUI(~dirt)
e = ~sdg.addInsert(0, \eq);
e.unit.highPassOn = true;
e.unit.highPassFreq = 120;
e.gui;

c = ~sdg.addInsert(0, \compressor);
c.unit.threshold = -24;
c.unit.ratio = 4;
c.gui;

m = ~sdg.addInsert(0, \insight);      // after both: what they made of the orbit
m.gui;

~sdg.moveInsert(m, 0);                // or before them: what came in
~sdg.removeInserts(0);
::
